  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116472",
      "title": "Controlling Route Resolver Execution",
      "lectureOrder": 294,
      "videoOrder": 280,
      "sourceHash": "d1974b0418ec63b1c842f6eaa862ae72bcd5829399c5003a360ef077ec4b6031",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.75,
          "end": 2.64,
          "en": "So you did now learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.64,
          "end": 6.93,
          "en": "how you can provide static and dynamic data to Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.93,
          "end": 9,
          "en": "and how you can use resolvers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9,
          "end": 12.123,
          "en": "to get your data fetching out of Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.38,
          "end": 15.3,
          "en": "Now, of course, in this application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.3,
          "end": 18,
          "en": "we don't just have our username",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18,
          "end": 22.26,
          "en": "that we could resolve outside of the UserTasksComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.26,
          "end": 24.66,
          "en": "but we also got those user routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.66,
          "end": 27.15,
          "en": "where I got a TasksComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.15,
          "end": 30.39,
          "en": "where we're using userTasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.39,
          "end": 35.01,
          "en": "and that's why I now also added the resolve property here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.01,
          "end": 39.09,
          "en": "and why I'm now using a resolveUserTasks function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.09,
          "end": 41.19,
          "en": "for fetching those tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.19,
          "end": 45.42,
          "en": "Now, attached you find the updated user.routes.ts file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.42,
          "end": 50.42,
          "en": "and you find the updated tasks.component TypeScript file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.85,
          "end": 53.1,
          "en": "where I cleaned up the Component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.1,
          "end": 55.8,
          "en": "to only rely on inputs in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.8,
          "end": 59.19,
          "en": "and where I added this resolver function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.19,
          "end": 62.82,
          "en": "which also takes the query parameters into account",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.82,
          "end": 66.09,
          "en": "to fetch the tasks for a selected user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.09,
          "end": 67.353,
          "en": "and to then sort them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.82,
          "end": 71.58,
          "en": "Now, when you do all that though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.58,
          "end": 74.46000000000001,
          "en": "if you are using the two files I attached,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.46000000000001,
          "end": 78.87,
          "en": "you'll note that the app does not work the way it should.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.87,
          "end": 80.55,
          "en": "If I navigate to a user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.55,
          "end": 82.95,
          "en": "and I try changing the query parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.95,
          "end": 87.45,
          "en": "by clicking this button, you see the tasks aren't updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.45,
          "end": 89.943,
          "en": "Their order doesn't change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.99,
          "end": 92.82,
          "en": "And I'm showing this on purpose",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.82,
          "end": 96.57,
          "en": "because the default behavior by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.57,
          "end": 101.57,
          "en": "is that these resolver functions will be re executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.72999999999999,
          "end": 104.25,
          "en": "if a route parameter changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.25,
          "end": 107.313,
          "en": "but not if a query parameter changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.27000000000001,
          "end": 110.78999999999999,
          "en": "That is a behavior you can change though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.78999999999999,
          "end": 115.77000000000001,
          "en": "by adding another property to your route configuration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.77000000000001,
          "end": 120.43,
          "en": "You can add the runGuardsAndResolvers property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 121.95,
          "end": 124.68299999999999,
          "en": "and set that to a string value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 125.55,
          "end": 127.14,
          "en": "You could set it to always,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.14,
          "end": 129.96,
          "en": "which does what its name applies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 129.96,
          "end": 131.25,
          "en": "If you set this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 131.25,
          "end": 134.79,
          "en": "the resolver functions will always be re executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 134.79,
          "end": 138.39,
          "en": "whenever anything happens to that route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 138.39,
          "end": 143.22,
          "en": "Or we could set it to paramsOrQueryParamsChange here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 143.22,
          "end": 146.61,
          "en": "which is the setting we want because this will ensure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 146.61,
          "end": 148.77,
          "en": "that this resolver function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 148.77,
          "end": 151.92000000000002,
          "en": "will be re executed by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 151.92000000000002,
          "end": 154.68,
          "en": "whenever our route parameters change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 154.68,
          "end": 157.293,
          "en": "or the query parameters change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 158.61,
          "end": 162.51,
          "en": "So with this setting added to this route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 162.51,
          "end": 166.32,
          "en": "this resolver will be called as intended.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 166.32,
          "end": 167.94,
          "en": "And if you now save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 167.94,
          "end": 171.27,
          "en": "you can see that as you navigate between different users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 171.27,
          "end": 173.52,
          "en": "different tasks are loaded,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 173.52,
          "end": 176.13,
          "en": "and now sorting all the works again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 176.13,
          "end": 179.38,
          "en": "and those query parameters are respected again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 180.36,
          "end": 184.11,
          "en": "simply because we now changed this setting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.11,
          "end": 187.023,
          "en": "And that's therefore also something you should know about.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
